91:// crd.3a: Resistance Attribute for each defensive aspect. Effective rating is
92:// read as dots + bonus directly off the live character document (this
93:// project's "effective ratings" convention, CLAUDE.md) — no client accessor
94:// is imported here, since public/js/data/accessors.js is browser-coupled
95:// (bloodlines cache, rule-engine cache) and unsuitable for server-side use.
96://
97:// crd.3a code review (external Codex, Pass 2/3a): a plain object's truthy
98:// lookup accepts inherited Object.prototype keys ('toString', 'constructor',
99:// '__proto__' all resolve truthily) as if they were valid aspects. ASPECT_KEYS
100:// is checked with .includes() below rather than indexed directly, so an
101:// off-enum value — inherited or not — always 400s before ASPECT_ATTR is ever
102:// touched.
103:const ASPECT_KEYS = ['mental', 'social', 'physical'];
104:const ASPECT_ATTR = { mental: 'Resolve', social: 'Composure', physical: 'Stamina' };
105:
106:function _attrEffective(character, attrName) {
107:  const a = character.attributes?.[attrName];
108:  return (a?.dots || 0) + (a?.bonus || 0);
109:}
110:
111:function _willpowerMax(character) {
112:  return _attrEffective(character, 'Resolve') + _attrEffective(character, 'Composure');
113:}
114:
115:// crd.3a AC5: narrow, explicitly-named 2-merit bonus lookup — Indomitable and
116:// Closed Book, the two merits the disposable mockup already proved correct.
117:// No generic merit-bonus-value field exists anywhere on the character
118:// document (see this story's own Dev Notes for the full gap analysis); a
119:// third merit needing a contest bonus is real future work for a new
120:// server/schemas/rules/ type, not an extension of this lookup.
121:function _meritBonus(merit) {
122:  if (merit.rule_key === 'indomitable') return 2;
123:  if (merit.rule_key === 'closed-book') return merit.rating || 0;
124:  return 0;
125:}
126:
127:// crd.4a: the at-Court City Status advantage gate. Short-circuits on the
128:// cheapest check first (power_name) so the overwhelming majority of
129:// /resolve calls (any non-power contest) never touch chapters/game_sessions/
130:// territories at all. Returns null when the gate is closed for this
